        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This should be drastically solved on latest `main` via a breaking change.\r\n\r\nResolving #714 by precisely manipulating `builtin.files` worked, but was somewhat limited. This was proved by this issue (that `git_files` didn't work) and that both `grep` / `grep_live` didn't work either (with files similar to position encoding). Plus the whole \"getting icon can not recognize the present path).\r\n\r\nThis whole issue could be resolved by using different, more robust position separator instead of \":\". The one commonly used in CLI tools is `\\0` (a.k.a. `\\000`, a.k.a. \"null character\"). However, this would be a breaking change. After much deliberation, I think it  is worth here.\r\n\r\nAnother positive side effect to changing from \":\" to \"\\0\" is freedom to choose a character that visually separates position coordinates. Even during writing 'mini.pick' I remember thinking that something like \"│\" (tall vertical line resulting in a continuous vertical line; used in box drawing) would be better. But there was no good reason to have it, as \":\" was used directly in string items. Now after 3ade3590490b377f38c2f424e90615ede5a273e1 (and f20d8cd3a116ef65f022797de064a044b217ff53 for 'mini.extra') the tall vertical line is used for positions and I think certain pickers (`grep_live`, `grep`, `lsp`) look better with it.\r\n\r\nAll in all, thanks again for the issue that had an impact beyond itself :)",
            "created_at": "2024-07-15T18:37:18Z",
